    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-memory-16: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.10";
    dc:description "The statement is a hypothesis about what consciousness is. Neural and behavioral correlates of uncertainty can be recorded, and they remain compatible with several rival theories. No existing dataset contains an observation that would confirm or refute this identification.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Uncertainty about memory could be proxied by metacognitive or physiological measures, but those measures would not distinguish this hypothesis from other theories that tie consciousness to uncertainty, prediction error, or internal monitoring.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Consciousness has no agreed measurement that would uniquely confirm this extension of Solms.", "Palpated uncertainty about memories is not separable from ordinary metacognition or recall failure.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.8"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.098"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
